p.src:
Linearity now gives the general free evolution as a Fourier superposition: $\boxed{
  \psi(x,t)
  =
  \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\hbar}}
  \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dp\,
  e^{ipx/\hbar}
  e^{-ip^2t/(2m\hbar)}
  \widetilde\psi(p).}$ The coefficient $\widetilde\psi(p)$ is the momentum-space amplitude at $t=0$. Every value of momentum evolves independently by the phase dictated by its energy.

