Fourier inversion then gives $\boxed{
  \widetilde\psi(p)
  =
  \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\hbar}}
  \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dx\,
  e^{-ipx/\hbar}\psi(x,0).}$ The factors of $\hbar$ have been kept explicit so that $px/\hbar$ is dimensionless and the two representations have compatible normalization.

