p.src:
The classical law for a phase-space function $K(x,p)$ is $\dot K=\{K,H\}_{\mathrm{PB}},$ where $\{A,B\}_{\mathrm{PB}}
  =
  \frac{\partial A}{\partial x}
  \frac{\partial B}{\partial p}
  -
  \frac{\partial A}{\partial p}
  \frac{\partial B}{\partial x}.$ The order in Equation  follows directly from the chain rule and Hamilton’s equations: $\begin{aligned}
  \dot K
  &=
  \frac{\partial K}{\partial x}\dot x
  +
  \frac{\partial K}{\partial p}\dot p\\
  &=
  \frac{\partial K}{\partial x}
  \frac{\partial H}{\partial p}
  -
  \frac{\partial K}{\partial p}
  \frac{\partial H}{\partial x}.\end{aligned}$

