p.src:
Both brackets are antisymmetric, $=-[B,A],
  \qquad
  \{A,B\}_{\mathrm{PB}}=-\{B,A\}_{\mathrm{PB}},$ and both act as derivations on products: $\begin{aligned}
&=A[B,C]+[A,C]B,
  \\
  \{AB,C\}_{\mathrm{PB}}
  &=A\{B,C\}_{\mathrm{PB}}
  +\{A,C\}_{\mathrm{PB}}B.
  \end{aligned}$ For classical functions the order of the ordinary factors is immaterial. For operators it is not, which is why the placement of $B$ in Equation  must be preserved.

