p.src:
Add a position-dependent potential: $\hat H=\frac{\hat p^{\,2}}{2m}+U(\hat x).$ In position space, $U(\hat x)$ acts by multiplication, and the Schrödinger equation becomes $i\hbar\frac{\partial\psi(x,t)}{\partial t}
  =
  \left[
    -\frac{\hbar^2}{2m}\frac{\partial^2}{\partial x^2}
    +U(x)
  \right]\psi(x,t).$ The associated force is $F(x)=-U'(x).$

